From: Xios Project <xios@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid WebKit X11 accessibility lookup on iOS Wayland

The GTK WebKit port is built with both X11 and Wayland support. On iOS it can
construct PlatformDisplayX11 without an X display while Epiphany is a native
Wayland client, then dereference the null display while looking up AT_SPI_BUS.
Supply a non-empty fallback address before WebKit starts. Preserve any real
AT-SPI address installed by the Xios accessibility bridge.

--- a/src/ephy-main.c
+++ b/src/ephy-main.c
@@ -180,0 +181,9 @@
+#ifdef __ENVIRONMENT_IPHONE_OS_VERSION_MIN_REQUIRED__
+  /*
+   * WebKitGTK 2.44's dual X11/Wayland build consults the X root-window
+   * AT_SPI_BUS property even when no X display exists. A real bridge address,
+   * when present, always wins over this disabled-bus fallback.
+   */
+  g_setenv ("AT_SPI_BUS_ADDRESS", "unix:path=/var/jb/tmp/xios-no-atspi", FALSE);
+#endif
+
